## Contract 1: GoldRefinery

### Role
The entry point. Takes USDC (from minting) and converts it to physical-gold-backed tokens (PAXG and XAUt).

### How It Works
1. Treasury sends USDC to this contract
2. Contract swaps 70% to PAXG, 30% to XAUt via Uniswap/Curve
3. Gold tokens are sent to GoldVault

### Why Latinum Needs It
| Without GoldRefinery | With GoldRefinery |
|---------------------|------------------|
| Mint USDC sits idle | USDC becomes gold reserves |
| No tangible backing | Verifiable gold backing |
| Treasury has to manually swap | Automated, auditable conversion |

### Interaction with Liquity Fork
GoldRefinery deposits into GoldVault. GoldVault is the collateral source for the CDP. So GoldRefinery *feeds* the CDP.

---

## Contract 2: GoldVault

### Role
The "Fort Knox." A secure holding contract with a one-way valve—gold can enter, but only the CDP can withdraw (and only for specific buyback scenarios).

### How It Works
- Only treasury can deposit gold
- Only the Internal CDP contract can withdraw gold (and only for buybacks when GPL trades below backing)
- Total gold value is tracked via Chainlink oracles

### Why Latinum Needs It
| Without GoldVault | With GoldVault |
|------------------|----------------|
| Gold held in EOA or simple wallet | Programmatic security |
| Team could withdraw anytime | One-way valve builds trust |
| No automated value tracking | Real-time gold value for CDP |

### Interaction with Liquity Fork
GoldVault is the **collateral source**. Your modified Liquity fork doesn't hold gold directly—it calls GoldVault to:
- Check collateral balance
- Lock gold when borrowing
- Unlock gold when repaying (or for buybacks)

This separation means the CDP logic is cleaner and gold custody is isolated.

---

## Contract 3: Internal CDP (Modified Liquity Fork)

### Role
The borrowing engine. Takes gold collateral and allows the treasury to borrow stablecoins (USDC) against it at 0% interest, with a conservative 25% LTV.

### How It Works
- Treasury calls `borrow(amount)`
- Contract checks GoldVault for collateral value
- Enforces LTV (max 25%) and collateral ratio (min 400%)
- Mints/transfers USDC to treasury
- Debt is tracked; repay calls reduce debt

### Why Latinum Needs It
| Without CDP | With CDP |
|------------|----------|
| Gold sits idle, illiquid | Gold becomes productive capital |
| Treasury must sell gold for liquidity | Treasury borrows against gold, keeps gold |
| No leverage for growth | Conservative leverage to fund LP, yield |

### How It Benefits Latinum Specifically
1. **Preserves gold backing** — You never sell the gold that backs GPL
2. **Funds GPL liquidity** — Borrowed USDC can seed GPL/USDC pools
3. **Creates flywheel** — LP fees → buy more gold → more borrowing capacity → more LP
4. **0% cost of capital** — No interest payments to external lenders

